From: ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T OpenBMC port
Subject: [PATCH] allow a mount point to present as a CD/DVD
Upstream-Status: Pending

lun.0/cdrom was hardcoded to "0", so every attached image enumerated as a
removable disk regardless of content. That makes the Redfish Cd boot override
unusable: the host BIOS classifies a boot entry from the device's SCSI
peripheral type, and IPMI boot device 0x05 (Force boot from default CD/DVD)
only resolves against an entry classified as CD/DVD. An ISO attached to a
cdrom=0 gadget is indistinguishable from a USB stick, so the override falls
through to the next device -- which looks exactly like it being ignored.

Add an optional per-mount-point "Cdrom" boolean and thread it to the gadget.
It defaults to false, so existing configurations are unaffected. DMTF models
MediaTypes as a property of the VirtualMedia resource rather than of the
inserted image, so a per-slot setting is the schema-correct shape; it also
avoids having to inspect image content over a possibly-remote nbd device
before the gadget can be configured.

The shipped virtual-media.json opts Slot_2 in, so the board has one CD-class
and one removable-class slot. Setting it here rather than shipping a near-copy
of this file from the layer keeps the two from drifting apart on an uprev.

diff --git a/src/configuration.hpp b/src/configuration.hpp
index efdddf2..9e37218 100644
--- a/src/configuration.hpp
+++ b/src/configuration.hpp
@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@ class Configuration
         std::optional<int> blocksize;
         std::chrono::seconds remainingInactivityTimeout;
         Mode mode;
+        // Present the gadget as a CD/DVD rather than a removable disk. The host
+        // BIOS classifies a boot entry from the device's SCSI peripheral type,
+        // so IPMI boot device 0x05 only resolves against a device reporting as
+        // one; with cdrom=0 an attached ISO is just another removable disk.
+        bool cdrom = false;
 
         static std::vector<std::string> toArgs(const MountPoint& mp)
         {
@@ -207,6 +212,7 @@ class Configuration
                                    "BlockSize not set, use default");
                         }
                     }
+                    mp.cdrom = mountpoint.value().value("Cdrom", false);
                     const auto modeIter = mountpoint.value().find("Mode");
                     if (modeIter != mountpoint.value().cend())
                     {
